        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Memphis, Shelby County, Tennessee, Albany, Dougherty County, Georgia, United States\n- Organizations: Memphis International Airport, Southwest Georgia Regional Airport\n- Concepts: Airport codes, civil-military airports, public-use airports, city-owned airports\n\nFacts:\n- Memphis International Airport has the airport codes IATA MEM, ICAO KMEM, and FAA LID MEM.\n- Memphis International Airport is a civil-military airport located seven miles southeast of downtown Memphis in Shelby County, Tennessee, United States.\n- Southwest Georgia Regional Airport has the airport codes IATA ABY, ICAO KABY, and FAA LID ABY.\n- Southwest Georgia Regional Airport is a city-owned, public-use airport located three nautical miles southwest of the central business district of Albany in Dougherty County, Georgia, United States.",
